  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 415 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nClear skies, light winds, & high pressure overhead have allowed \ntemperatures to fall into the mid 30s across portions of \ncentral Minnesota & western Wisconsin early this morning. A \nFrost Advisory remains in effect through 9 AM, with frost most \nlikely in rural  low-lying areas through sunrise. Temperatures \nrebound quickly this morning as southeasterly winds increase, \nwith highs reaching the mid to upper 60s this afternoon. Upper\nlevel forcing increases late this afternoon & evening from a\ncombination of an approaching jetstreak & weak ripple of\nvorticity passing through northern Minnesota. Enough forcing \nlooks to be present to generate some scattered light rain \nshowers this evening, primarily north of Interstate 94 across \ncentral Minnesota & west-central Wisconsin.\n\nWell-above normal temperatures are expected Tuesday as \nshortwave ridging briefly builds over the upper Midwest, & \nbreezy dry southwest winds lead to deep surface mixing. Highs in\nthe low 80s looks possible across southwest Minnesota & could \nreach 80 into the Twin Cities metro. Cooler air returns \nfollowing a frontal passage Tuesday night bringing a modest \ncool- down for Wednesday through Friday, although highs will \nremain right near seasonal norms in the mid to upper 60s. \nSoutherly flow then returns for next weekend, allowing \ntemperatures to climb back into the 70s. Dry weather looks to \npersists into next weekend as upper level ridging generally \npredominates over the central CONUS.",
